# Generated dataset
# Deterministically regenerable from db/generate_dataset.py + a seed (verified
# byte-identical across runs, including under a changed PYTHONHASHSEED), so none
# of it belongs in history -- and history is forever even after a later delete.
# Currently 2.2 GB; the full spec-scale sweep projects to ~24-27 GB
# (docs/phase0_power_check.md §7).
db/csv/

# The v1-preset fixture db/csv/ held before the Phase 6 spec-scale sweep. Parked
# rather than deleted; regenerable in ~10 s per variant-seed with `--config v1`
# and verified byte-identical during that session, so it is safe to `rm -rf`.
db/csv_v1preset_superseded/

# The V1-comparable builds the Phase 7 training sweep runs on (12 variants x 5
# seeds at `--config v1`, 2.2 GB). Same argument as db/csv/: deterministically
# regenerable, so none of it belongs in history.
db/csv_v1scale/

# Mid-scale (sup_n=2,000) builds for the Layer 3 discovery check, where the v1
# preset lacks the statistical power to support it. Regenerable; see
# reports/layer3_testing.md section 2.2.
db/csv_mid/

# V3 schema-enrichment builds (`--enrich`): the v1-preset worlds re-emitted with
# db/enrich_schema.py's Carrier/Port/Route/replenishment tables added. Same
# argument as every other build above -- deterministically regenerable, ~18 s per
# variant-seed with
#   python3 db/generate_dataset.py --variant 0 --seed <s> --config v1 --enrich
# and db/verify_enriched.py asserts the 20 pre-existing tables come out
# BYTE-IDENTICAL to a non-enriched build, so the enriched directory is a strict,
# reproducible superset rather than a distinct artifact. 212 MB for the five
# seeds; see reports/new_nodes_result.md section 1.
db/csv_v3enriched/

# ML harness working files: the snapshot-assembly cache (large, derived) and the
# training results. Results JSONs carry the raw test predictions so paired
# comparisons can be recomputed without retraining -- useful, but megabytes per
# run and regenerable. The REPORT is what gets committed (docs/phase7_*.md).
ml/.cache/
out/

# resolved_config.json lives inside db/csv/ and is excluded with it. It is small,
# but it carries a `generated_at` timestamp, so it churns on every regeneration
# even when nothing else changed, and a full sweep produces 60 of them. To
# preserve the manifest of a *published* run, copy that one file into docs/ --
# a deliberate archival act rather than incidental tracking.

# Ad-hoc transfer/scratch archives at the repo root. Not produced by any script
# in this repository and not reproducible from it, so they are working files
# rather than artifacts -- currently ~1.1 GB of them. Anchored to the root so a
# legitimately named file deeper in the tree is unaffected.
/_tmp_*

# Database dumps and backups
# Defensive: V2 has no reports/backups/ directory and calls no pg_dump today, but
# db/load_data.py drives a live PostgreSQL instance and HADES_v1 kept dumps here.
reports/backups/
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.sql.bak
